  "context": "Implementation is committed and published to the existing implementation PR. Local worktree /Users/joe/Developer/BenchBox.wt-release-process: branch fix/release-cut-origin-head-linked-worktree, exact HEAD 29aa047e910b5bea87c99d498a52418b1c475d94, origin branch matches, based on origin/develop 435d07e97c2e0f30a002d721fbc42aca508d6a52; clean. Commit 76afd92a2 fixes the abort path for a worktree holding develop; commit 29aa047e rejects stale origin/develop resumes and local tag ambiguity and parses full refs to handle same-name branch/tag cases. Focused release-cut file passed 21 tests. Canonical make pr-preflight finished at 2026-09-24T01:42:30Z with ordered_success on exact HEAD 29aa047e; both local-focused-check and required-pr-preflight executed with exit_code 0, and medium-tier executed with exit_code 0 (2,111 passed, 21 skipped). make pr-open updated https://github.com/BenchBox-dev/BenchBox/pull/2318; PR is OPEN/non-draft/mergeable at exact head 29aa047e, hosted checks are still running. Live review threads: P1 accepting the finalizer gap is covered by OPEN PR #2321 and remains unresolved until that fix lands; P2 abort finding is outdated by 76afd92a2 and remains without a hosted reply or resolution. No release was cut. Next: wait for hosted checks, re-read every thread/check on exact head, and keep this TODO active until the implementation PR merges.",
  "description": "Make the existing release-cut target usable under BenchBox's linked-worktree policy and reject unreviewed or omitted source commits. Prior art: make worktree-create fetches origin/develop, creates an allowed named branch, pins identity, and records its base (scripts/worktree_lifecycle.sh:136-185); release-cut currently accepts only local develop or vX.Y.Z, fetches origin, then branches from local develop (Makefile:1074-1098). Extend the existing target rather than adding a parallel release command. For a new cut, fetch origin before deciding eligibility, require a clean linked checkout whose HEAD equals the fetched origin/develop commit, and create vX.Y.Z from that exact commit. Preserve the current guarded resume behavior for an uncommitted vX.Y.Z cut. Decision: whether to allow only a worktree-create branch or any clean linked-worktree branch at that exact SHA; choose the smallest rule compatible with the existing worktree metadata and preflight. Keep release version explicit. Do not write in the primary clone, loosen agent-write-preflight, bypass required release checks, reset unrelated work, or force-push protected refs. The next release operator must choose a version only after checking the existing v0.4.1 branch and PyPI/tag state.",
